cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "prodrome: a signal-to-label latency engine for FDA adverse event data"
message: "If you use this software or its method, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "S"
    given-names: "Mithin Sagar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mithinsagar/prodrome"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
keywords:
  - pharmacovigilance
  - disproportionality analysis
  - signal detection
  - FAERS
  - structured product labeling
  - survival analysis
abstract: >
  prodrome measures how much lead time pharmacovigilance signal-detection criteria
  buy before a drug's label changes. It reconstructs each drug's full labelling
  history from the DailyMed SPL archive, recomputes disproportionality statistics
  point-in-time at every quarter boundary using only reports FDA had received by that
  date, and reports the lead time each published criterion achieved against the label
  change that followed. It also quantifies the contamination that conventional
  retrospective analyses incur: because reporting of a reaction rises after it is
  added to a label, a statistic computed on the full cumulative database is partly
  caused by the outcome it would be used to predict.
